<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Phaltan State</h1><p class="st-meta">1284 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Phaltan</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Deccan fief of the Nimbalkar family, one of the oldest Maratha houses, into which Shivaji married and which survived as a princely state until 1948.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nimbalkar">Nimbalkars</a> claim to have held Phaltan since the late 13th century, and they are counted among the oldest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> families. In the 16th and 17th centuries they served the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/bijapur-sultanate">Bijapur Sultanate</a> as military chiefs.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saibai">Saibai Nimbalkar</a> of Phaltan became the first wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a>, linking the family to the founder of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a>. Phaltan later held its lands under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satara">Satara</a> rulers and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwas</a>. After 1818 it came under British protection as one of the Satara <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagir">jagirs</a> and then the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-states-agency">Deccan States Agency</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Phaltan merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bombay-state">Bombay State</a> in 1948. Its last ruler, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malojirao-nimbalkar">Malojirao Nimbalkar</a>, went on to serve as a minister in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumbai">Bombay</a>. The town is now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satara">Satara</a> district, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/phaltan-state.jpg" alt="Phaltan State" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Robert Alfers · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Phaltan_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1284 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Phaltan</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Malojirao Nimbalkar</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Marathi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Phaltan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1616&amp;focus=phaltan-state" aria-label="Phaltan State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6815 1510 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Phaltan State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7135 1766L6991 1757M7135 1766L7364 1601M7135 1766L7364 1602M7135 1766L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6991 1757h0M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7135 1766h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7135 1766h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1616&amp;focus=phaltan-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
